        "Nothing",
        "A full stop ."
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "Every if, else (and later loops and functions) header ends with a colon."
    },
    {
      "q": "How does Python know which lines belong to the if?",
      "options": [
        "They are indented under it",
        "They are in brackets",
        "They come right after it, until a blank line",
        "They end with a colon"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "Indentation (4 spaces) marks the block. Python has no brackets for blocks."
    },
    {
      "q": "In an if/else, how many of the two blocks run?",
      "options": [
        "Exactly one",
        "Both",
